<main class="min-h-screen">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-base-content mb-4">
        {gettext("Workflows")}
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Stride wraps every task in a four-stage lifecycle. Humans choose when to be involved and when to allow the agent to work independently. The board drives a real codebase, not a vibe."
        )}
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center">
        {gettext("Requirements")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {raw(
          String.replace(
            gettext(
              "Before a single task hits the board, stride-ideation turns a fuzzy idea into a structured plan. An interactive session writes a committed requirements document, then decomposes it into a goal with dependency-ordered tasks — so agents start from a real specification, not a one-line prompt."
            ),
            "stride-ideation",
            ~s{<a href="https://github.com/cheezy/stride-ideation" class="underline" style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">stride-ideation</a>},
            global: false
          )
        )}
      </p>

      <div class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="text-center">
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {gettext("01")}
            </div>
            <code class="text-base font-mono font-semibold text-base-content">/ideate</code>
            <div class="text-xs mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
              {gettext(
                "An interactive Q&A turns a fuzzy idea into a committed requirements doc — Goal, Problem, Outcome, Assumptions, Constraints, Non-goals, Success Metrics."
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {gettext("02")}
            </div>
            <code class="text-base font-mono font-semibold text-base-content">/stridify</code>
            <div class="text-xs mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
              {gettext(
                "Decomposes that document into a goal with dependency-ordered tasks, each sized to roughly 5 to 15 minutes of work."
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {gettext("03")}
            </div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("On the board")}</div>
            <div class="text-xs mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
              {gettext(
                "The goal and its tasks land in the Backlog. Once a human moves them to Ready, agents claim them and the lifecycle below takes over."
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <img
        src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-requirements.png"}
        alt={gettext("A goal with its three child tasks and the column each one is in")}
        width="1176"
        height="586"
        loading="lazy"
        class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
        style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
      />
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center">
        {gettext("Getting ready for development")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Ideation fills the Backlog, but agents never touch it directly. A human curates first: review what was captured, decide which tasks need a human sign-off, and promote the ready work into the Ready column."
        )}
      </p>

      <div class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="text-center">
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {gettext("01")}
            </div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Review the Backlog")}</div>
            <div class="text-xs mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
              {gettext(
                "Humans read through the captured tasks, sharpen scope, and confirm each one has a clear reason and acceptance criteria before any agent sees it."
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {gettext("02")}
            </div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-base-content">
              {gettext("Decide what needs review")}
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
              {gettext(
                "Flag the tasks whose finished work should pause for human approval. Those stop in Review when complete; the rest advance straight to Done."
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {gettext("03")}
            </div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Move to Ready")}</div>
            <div class="text-xs mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
              {gettext(
                "Drag the prepared tasks into Ready. That move is the go signal — agents claim only from Ready, so nothing starts until a human says so."
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-8">
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-ready.png"}
          alt={gettext("The Backlog and Ready columns of a Stride board")}
          width="862"
          height="412"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 575px;"
        />
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-needs-review.png"}
          alt={gettext("The Needs Review checkbox on a task's form")}
          width="1236"
          height="276"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 824px;"
        />
      </div>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Backlog is the human staging area; Ready is the contract. Curating the board up front is what lets agents run autonomously once the lifecycle below kicks in."
        )}
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center">
        {gettext("The AI development lifecycle")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-6" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "When an agent claims a task from Ready, the card moves to Doing and the agent runs the Stride workflow — a fixed loop where hooks, subagents, and skills carry the work from claim to completion."
        )}
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mb-6 text-xs">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full" style="background: var(--st-doing);"></span>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">{gettext("Hook")}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full" style="background: var(--stride-violet);"></span>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">{gettext("Subagent")}</span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-8 mb-6">
        <ol class="space-y-5">
          <li>
            <details class="group rounded-lg -mx-2 px-2 py-1.5 hover:bg-base-200/60 transition-colors">
              <summary class="flex gap-4 items-start cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
                <div
                  class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide pt-0.5 w-6 shrink-0"
                  style="color: var(--ink-2);"
                >
                  {gettext("01")}
                </div>
                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Claim")}</span>
                    <span
                      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0 text-[11px] font-medium"
                      style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink);"
                    >
                      {gettext("Details")}
                      <.icon
                        name="hero-chevron-down"
                        class="h-3.5 w-3.5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                      />
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-xs mt-0.5" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                    {gettext("The agent claims a task from Ready; the card moves to Doing.")}
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-2">
                    <span
                      class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]"
                      style="background: var(--st-doing-soft); color: var(--st-doing);"
                    >
                      before_doing
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 pl-10 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                {raw(
                  String.replace(
                    gettext(
                      "When the agent claims the task, the card moves to the Doing column and the developer-defined before_doing hook runs on the developer's workstation. This developer hook is typically used to make sure the local checkout is up to date with the latest code, fetch the latest dependencies, apply any necessary database migrations, and run the tests — so the agent starts from a known state."
                    ),
                    "before_doing",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--st-doing);">before_doing</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                )}
              </div>
              <figure class="mt-4 sm:pl-10">
                <img
                  src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-claim.png"}
                  alt={gettext("The Doing column with two tasks in progress")}
                  width="420"
                  height="326"
                  loading="lazy"
                  class="block max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
                  style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 280px;"
                />
              </figure>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="group rounded-lg -mx-2 px-2 py-1.5 hover:bg-base-200/60 transition-colors">
              <summary class="flex gap-4 items-start cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
                <div
                  class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide pt-0.5 w-6 shrink-0"
                  style="color: var(--ink-2);"
                >
                  {gettext("02")}
                </div>
                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Explore")}</span>
                    <span
                      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0 text-[11px] font-medium"
                      style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink);"
                    >
                      {gettext("Details")}
                      <.icon
                        name="hero-chevron-down"
                        class="h-3.5 w-3.5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                      />
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-xs mt-0.5" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                    {gettext(
                      "A subagent maps the key files, related tests, and existing patterns before any code is written."
                    )}
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-2">
                    <span
                      class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]"
                      style="background: var(--stride-violet-soft); color: var(--stride-violet-ink);"
                    >
                      task-explorer
                    </span>
                    <span
                      class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]"
                      style="background: var(--stride-violet-soft); color: var(--stride-violet-ink);"
                    >
                      planner
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </summary>
              <div
                class="mt-3 pl-10 text-xs leading-relaxed space-y-2"
                style="color: var(--ink-2);"
              >
                <p>
                  {raw(
                    String.replace(
                      gettext(
                        "The task-explorer subagent goes first. It reads the files the task flags as relevant, finds the tests that cover them, and searches the codebase for the existing patterns and surrounding context the work should follow. It hands back a structured summary — what already exists, which conventions to mirror, and what can be reused — so the implementing agent starts with a map of the codebase rather than a blank page."
                      ),
                      "task-explorer",
                      ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--stride-violet-ink);">task-explorer</span>|,
                      global: false
                    )
                  )}
                </p>
                <p>
                  {raw(
                    String.replace(
                      gettext(
                        "For medium and larger tasks, a planner subagent then turns that map into a plan. Using the explorer's findings alongside the task's acceptance criteria, testing strategy, and known pitfalls, it outlines the implementation step by step, calls out which files will change, and weighs any architectural trade-offs before a single line of code is written."
                      ),
                      "planner",
                      ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--stride-violet-ink);">planner</span>|,
                      global: false
                    )
                  )}
                </p>
              </div>
              <figure class="mt-4 sm:pl-10">
                <img
                  src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-explore.png"}
                  alt={gettext("The explorer's result in a task's details")}
                  width="792"
                  height="272"
                  loading="lazy"
                  class="block max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
                  style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 528px;"
                />
                <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                  {gettext(
                    "The task's details record the explorer's result: whether it ran, how long it took, and its summary."
                  )}
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="group rounded-lg -mx-2 px-2 py-1.5 hover:bg-base-200/60 transition-colors">
              <summary class="flex gap-4 items-start cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
                <div
                  class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide pt-0.5 w-6 shrink-0"
                  style="color: var(--ink-2);"
                >
                  {gettext("03")}
                </div>
                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Implement")}</span>
                    <span
                      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0 text-[11px] font-medium"
                      style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink);"
                    >
                      {gettext("Details")}
                      <.icon
                        name="hero-chevron-down"
                        class="h-3.5 w-3.5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                      />
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-xs mt-0.5" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                    {gettext("The agent writes the code to complete the task.")}
                  </div>
                </div>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 pl-10 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                {raw(
                  gettext(
                    "The implementing agent now writes the code, drawing on everything gathered so far: the task specification carried in the Stride claim — its acceptance criteria, pitfalls, and the human-reviewed details — the task-explorer's map of the existing files, tests, and patterns, and, on medium and larger tasks, the planner's step-by-step plan. It writes both the implementation and the tests that exercise it, mirroring the conventions the explorer surfaced so the change fits cleanly into the codebase it lands in."
                  )
                  |> String.replace(
                    "task-explorer",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--stride-violet-ink);">task-explorer</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                  |> String.replace(
                    "planner",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--stride-violet-ink);">planner</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                )}
              </div>
              <figure class="mt-4 sm:pl-10">
                <img
                  src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-implement.png"}
                  alt={gettext("A finished task's changed files with one file's diff open")}
                  width="776"
                  height="580"
                  loading="lazy"
                  class="block max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
                  style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 517px;"
                />
              </figure>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="group rounded-lg -mx-2 px-2 py-1.5 hover:bg-base-200/60 transition-colors">
              <summary class="flex gap-4 items-start cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
                <div
                  class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide pt-0.5 w-6 shrink-0"
                  style="color: var(--ink-2);"
                >
                  {gettext("04")}
                </div>
                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Review")}</span>
                    <span
                      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0 text-[11px] font-medium"
                      style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink);"
                    >
                      {gettext("Details")}
                      <.icon
                        name="hero-chevron-down"
                        class="h-3.5 w-3.5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                      />
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-xs mt-0.5" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                    {gettext(
                      "A subagent checks the diff against the task's acceptance criteria and pitfalls."
                    )}
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-2">
                    <span
                      class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]"
                      style="background: var(--stride-violet-soft); color: var(--stride-violet-ink);"
                    >
                      task-reviewer
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 pl-10 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                {raw(
                  gettext(
                    "The task-reviewer subagent checks the finished diff against the task's own contract — its acceptance criteria, pitfalls, patterns to follow, and testing strategy — catching the task-specific problems that automated tests can't. It also enforces the project's standing rules: when a CODE-REVIEW.md file is present, each bullet in it becomes a review check — a CRITICAL: prefix raising its severity — and any unmet check is treated just like a task-specific finding. When the review comes back clean, the work moves straight on to validation. When it surfaces critical or important issues, the implementing agent fixes them and the diff is reviewed again; only once those are resolved does the task advance, while minor suggestions are noted but never block."
                  )
                  |> String.replace(
                    "task-reviewer",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--stride-violet-ink);">task-reviewer</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                  |> String.replace(
                    "CODE-REVIEW.md",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono">CODE-REVIEW.md</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                )}
              </div>
              <figure class="mt-4 sm:pl-10">
                <div class="space-y-4">
                  <img
                    src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-review-report.png"}
                    alt={gettext("The task-reviewer's report with one minor issue")}
                    width="792"
                    height="592"
                    loading="lazy"
                    class="block max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
                    style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 528px;"
                  />
                  <img
                    src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-review-matrix.png"}
                    alt={
                      gettext(
                        "A task's behaviour test matrix with a test and a status for each behaviour"
                      )
                    }
                    width="796"
                    height="854"
                    loading="lazy"
                    class="block max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
                    style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 531px;"
                  />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                  {gettext(
                    "The task's details show the task-reviewer's report and, when the board's field visibility settings turn it on, the task's behaviour test matrix: each behaviour, the test that covers it, and its status."
                  )}
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="group rounded-lg -mx-2 px-2 py-1.5 hover:bg-base-200/60 transition-colors">
              <summary class="flex gap-4 items-start cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
                <div
                  class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide pt-0.5 w-6 shrink-0"
                  style="color: var(--ink-2);"
                >
                  {gettext("05")}
                </div>
                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Validate")}</span>
                    <span
                      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0 text-[11px] font-medium"
                      style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink);"
                    >
                      {gettext("Details")}
                      <.icon
                        name="hero-chevron-down"
                        class="h-3.5 w-3.5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                      />
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-xs mt-0.5" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                    {gettext("Developer defined validations that must pass before completion.")}
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-2">
                    <span
                      class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]"
                      style="background: var(--st-doing-soft); color: var(--st-doing);"
                    >
                      after_doing
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 pl-10 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                {raw(
                  gettext(
                    "Validation runs the after_doing hook — a blocking quality gate whose commands the developer defines. They typically run the full test suite, check formatting, run static code analysis, and run a security scan, and often build the project and auto-commit the change. Because the hook blocks completion, any failure stops the task cold: the agent fixes what broke and re-runs the hook until everything passes, so nothing reaches Done in a broken state."
                  )
                  |> String.replace(
                    "after_doing",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--st-doing);">after_doing</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                  |> String.replace(
                    ".stride.md",
                    ~s|<span class="font-mono">.stride.md</span>|,
                    global: false
                  )
                )}
              </div>
              <figure class="mt-4 sm:pl-10">
                <img
                  src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-validate.png"}
                  alt={gettext("The workflow steps a task recorded, including After Doing")}
                  width="792"
                  height="394"
                  loading="lazy"
                  class="block max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
                  style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 528px;"
                />
                <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
                  {gettext(
                    "When the task is completed, the steps the agent ran, the after_doing hook among them, are recorded under Workflow steps in the task's details."
                  )}
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </details>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center">
        {gettext("Human review and completion")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {raw(
          gettext(
            "When the agent marks a task complete, the before_review hook fires — the moment to open a pull request, post the diff for reviewers, or ping a channel. What happens next turns on a single flag a human set back in the Backlog: needs_review."
          )
          |> String.replace(
            "before_review",
            ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--st-doing);">before_review</span>|,
            global: false
          )
          |> String.replace(
            "needs_review",
            ~s|<span class="font-mono">needs_review</span>|,
            global: false
          )
        )}
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
        <div class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-base-content mb-2">{gettext("Flagged for review")}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {raw(
              gettext(
                "A task with needs_review set to true lands in the Review column and stops. It surfaces in the review queue — the shared list of finished tasks awaiting a human — which shows a full diff of every changed file alongside the task-reviewer's report. The reviewer reads through it and then approves the task or requests changes. On approval the after_review hook fires — merge, deploy, notify — and the task moves to Done."
              )
              |> String.replace(
                "needs_review",
                ~s|<span class="font-mono">needs_review</span>|,
                global: false
              )
              |> String.replace(
                "task-reviewer",
                ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--stride-violet-ink);">task-reviewer</span>|,
                global: false
              )
              |> String.replace(
                "after_review",
                ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--st-doing);">after_review</span>|,
                global: false
              )
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-base-content mb-2">{gettext("Cleared to ship")}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {raw(
              gettext(
                "A task without that flag never pauses. It moves straight to Done, the after_review hook fires immediately — the same merge-and-deploy step, with no human in the loop — and the change is shipped on the spot."
              )
              |> String.replace(
                "after_review",
                ~s|<span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--st-doing);">after_review</span>|,
                global: false
              )
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-8">
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-flagged-for-review.png"}
          alt={gettext("The review queue with a waiting task's diff")}
          width="1196"
          height="748"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/workflows-cleared-to-ship.png"}
          alt={gettext("The Review and Done columns of a Stride board")}
          width="856"
          height="474"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line); width: 571px;"
        />
      </div>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "And the agent doesn't wait around. As soon as an un-flagged task reaches Done, it claims the next task from the Ready column and runs the whole loop again — working straight through the board until Ready is empty. Only a task that needs human review pauses the run, holding in the Review column until someone signs off."
        )}
      </p>
    </section>

    <%!-- Setup (W2461): the runtimes with a Stride plugin, the .stride.md hook
    file and the quality gates. Copy is plain gettext with no raw/1: hook and
    agent names sit in their own <code> elements. --%>
    <section id="runtimes" class="mb-16" aria-labelledby="runtimes-heading">
      <h2 id="runtimes-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center">
        {gettext("Works with your agent")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Stride has a plugin for six agent runtimes. Each one teaches the agent the same loop: claim a task, run the hooks in your .stride.md and complete the work."
        )}
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div
          :for={runtime <- workflow_runtimes()}
          data-runtime={runtime.key}
          class="min-w-0 bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-5"
        >
          <h3 class="font-semibold">
            <a
              href={runtime.url}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >{runtime.name}</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">{runtime.install}</p>
        </div>
        <div
          data-runtime="mcp"
          class="min-w-0 sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3 bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-base-300 p-5"
        >
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-base-content">{gettext("Any MCP client")}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "No plugin for your tool? Stride's MCP server gives any MCP client the same task loop as six tools, using the same API token as the REST API. MCP is part of the paid plans."
            )}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            <.link
              href={~p"/resources/connecting-an-mcp-client"}
              class="font-medium underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >
              {gettext("Read the guide: Connecting an MCP client")}
            </.link>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="hooks" class="mb-16" aria-labelledby="hooks-heading">
      <h2 id="hooks-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center">
        {gettext("Your hooks, in one file")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Hooks are shell commands you keep in a .stride.md file at the root of your project. The agent runs each one on your own machine at a fixed point in the loop. When a command fails, the agent stops there and fixes the problem before it carries on."
        )}
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <pre
            tabindex="0"
            aria-label={gettext("An example .stride.md with all five hooks")}
            class="max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl p-5 text-left text-sm leading-relaxed"
            style="background: var(--surface-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink);"
          ><code class="font-mono">{stride_md_snippet()}</code></pre>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "Each section is a heading and a bash block. The commands are yours: use whatever your project already runs."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <dl class="min-w-0 space-y-4">
          <div :for={{hook, purpose} <- workflow_hooks()}>
            <dt>
              <.workflow_pill kind={:hook}>{hook}</.workflow_pill>
            </dt>
            <dd class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">{purpose}</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="quality-gates" class="mb-16" aria-labelledby="quality-gates-heading">
      <h2
        id="quality-gates-heading"
        class="text-2xl font-bold text-base-content mb-6 text-center"
      >
        {gettext("The quality gates around the code")}
      </h2>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-6" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Around the code the agent writes, the plugin adds gates in a fixed order. Small tasks can skip exploring and review, and the optional gates run only when their plugin is installed and the task asks for them."
        )}
      </p>

      <ol
        aria-label={gettext("The quality gates in the order they run")}
        class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 mb-4"
      >
        <li
          :for={{label, kind, last?} <- workflow_gate_chain()}
          class="flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <.workflow_pill :if={kind != :step} kind={kind}>{label}</.workflow_pill>
          <span
            :if={kind == :step}
            class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-semibold bg-base-200 text-base-content"
          >
            {label}
          </span>
          <span :if={!last?} aria-hidden="true" class="inline-flex" style="color: var(--ink-3);">
            <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0" />
          </span>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mb-6 text-xs">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full" style="background: var(--st-doing);"></span>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">{gettext("Hook")}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full" style="background: var(--stride-violet);"></span>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">{gettext("Subagent")}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span
            class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full border border-dashed"
            style="border-color: var(--stride-violet-ink);"
          ></span>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">{gettext("Optional plugin")}</span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-6 md:p-8">
        <ol class="space-y-5">
          <li
            :for={
              {{gate, pills, title, optional?, body}, index} <-
                Enum.with_index(workflow_quality_gates(), 1)
            }
            data-gate={gate}
            class="flex gap-4"
          >
            <div
              class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wide pt-0.5 w-6 shrink-0"
              style="color: var(--ink-2);"
            >
              {String.pad_leading(Integer.to_string(index), 2, "0")}
            </div>
            <div class="min-w-0">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-base-content flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                <span>{title}</span>
                <.workflow_pill :for={{pill, kind} <- pills} kind={kind}>{pill}</.workflow_pill>
                <span
                  :if={optional?}
                  class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide font-medium"
                  style="color: var(--ink-3);"
                >
                  {gettext("Optional")}
                </span>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1" style="color: var(--ink-2);">{body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-8 md:p-12 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-base-content mb-4">
        {gettext("Wire your project to Stride")}
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-6 max-w-xl mx-auto" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Drop a .stride.md in your project folder, get an API token for your agent, and watch the loop run on your own machine."
        )}
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center">
        <.link
          href={~p"/users/register"}
          class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-semibold hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
        >
          {gettext("Start now")}
        </.link>
        <.link
          href={~p"/resources"}
          class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg border-2 border-base-300 text-base-content font-semibold hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors"
        >
          {gettext("Read more details")}
        </.link>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
